<h1 id="qimpl-title" style="color:#0d47a1;font-size:1.5em;font-weight:700;border-bottom:2px solid #90caf9;padding-bottom:0.25em;margin-top:0"><code>qimpl</code> — quick implement (plan → execute → summarize)</h1>

Use when the user includes **`qimpl`**. Runs **one continuous engagement**: clarify blockers → author/update plan(s) → **`aciub`** every phase → closing layman table.

**Do not mix chains:** use **`qimpltdd`** for TDD chain 2 (see [execution chain](#qimpl-chain)).

---

<h2 id="qimpl-outline" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">Document outline</h2>

1. [Trigger](#qimpl-trigger) — keyword and scope.
2. [Step 1 — Ambiguity gate](#qimpl-step1) — multiple-choice or proceed.
3. [Step 2 — Plan authoring](#qimpl-step2) — **onlyref** delegate.
4. [Step 3 — Implement all phases](#qimpl-step3) — **aciub** delegate.
5. [Step 4 — Closing summary](#qimpl-step4) — layman table.
6. [Execution chain (classic)](#qimpl-chain) — explicit rule paths.
7. [Stop conditions](#qimpl-stop) — when pausing is allowed.
