<h2 id="qimpl-trigger" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">1. Trigger</h2>

| User says | Agent does |
|-----------|------------|
| **`qimpl`** + task description (no plan yet) | Steps 1 → 2 (new plan) → 3 → 4. |
| **`qimpl`** + existing plan **`.md` path** | Step 1 → 2 (refresh plan if gaps) → 3 on that path → 4. |
| **`qimpl`** + plan in **`wip/`** with partial `[X]` | Step 1 (if new ambiguity) → 3 resume → 4. |

If scope spans multiple independent refactors, split into **one plan per coherent strand** under **`cursor_gen/refactor_plans/new/`** (or update existing plans) — still **`aciub`** each plan to completion before stopping.

---

<h2 id="qimpl-step1" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">2. Step 1 — Ambiguity gate</h2>

Before plan or code work:

1. Scan the user request + relevant repo context for **product / schema / scope** decisions only **the user** can make.
2. **If true blockers remain:** stop and ask via **concise multiple-choice questions** (use **AskQuestion** when available — small groups, precise options, include a sensible default/recommended option). **Do not** start steps 2–3 until answered.
3. **If none remain:** state **“No blocking ambiguities”** in one line and **proceed immediately** to step 2 — no permission ask.

**Not ambiguities (decide and continue):** preferred defaults already in thread, plan, or docs; DRY/test placement; file paths inferable from codebase; heuristic TDD vs smoke-after-delete when using **`qimpltdd`**.

---

<h2 id="qimpl-step2" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. Step 2 — Plan authoring</h2>

**Read and execute** full **onlyref** procedure from:

**`.cursor/rules/onlyref-refactor-plan-author-only.mdc`**

**Additional requirements for `qimpl` plans:**

| Area | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| **Context** | Read applicable existing refactor plans, READMEs, and domain docs; cross-link sources; avoid duplicating completed work. |
| **Phases** | Sensible numbered stages; each phase ends with **verifiable** deliverables. |
| **Quality bar** | Per phase: code changes, **tests**, and the **implref** comments-and-docs gate (**cdcm**: file headers; **≥1 doc line per class and per function/method** in touched files; non-obvious inline notes; README / spec / `.env.example` — implref step 2 and §3.2b). Keep **DRY** (extract shared helpers/components before a third copy). |
| **Tests per stage** | Name **concrete** test files/commands at phase end: unit, integration, Vitest, Playwright **mocked `test:e2e`**, and **real/mock LLM e2e** when behavior crosses LM or live tiers (see **`.cursor/rules/project_specific/eellm-e2e-real-llm-runner.mdc`** when applicable). |
| **Location** | New plans: **`cursor_gen/refactor_plans/new/REFACTOR_*.md`** only (**onlyref** folder rule). |

When step 2 finishes, **do not** ask to proceed — start step 3 in the **same session**.

---

<h2 id="qimpl-step3" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Step 3 — Implement all phases</h2>

**Read and execute** full **aciub** procedure from:

**`.cursor/rules/aciub-allow-continue-iterations-until-blocked.mdc`**

against **every** plan produced or updated in step 2 (named path(s)).

| Rule | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| **Continuous** | Run **`aciub <plan.md>`** through **all** phases and open sidetracks — **no** mid-plan permission prompts. |
| **Delegate** | **aciub** pulls in **implref** / **resumimpl** per classic chain ([§6](#qimpl-chain)). |
| **Tests** | Honor each phase’s Quality bar; fix failures before marking `[X]`. |
| **Exwar** | Mandatory per **aciub** after each phase — not optional under **`qimpl`**. |

Only stop step 3 for **true blockers** ([§7](#qimpl-stop)) — not because work is large or multi-phase.

---

<h2 id="qimpl-step4" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">5. Step 4 — Closing summary</h2>

When step 3 completes or hits a stop condition, reply with a **SUPER concise layman HTML table** (MRKD 6.1: dark blue header, short cells):

| Row (suggested) | Content |
|-----------------|---------|
| **What we did** | One-line plain-language outcome |
| **Plans** | Final path(s) (`new/` / `wip/` / `completed/`) |
| **Tests** | What ran green (brief) |
| **War stories** | New **#N** or explicit skip per **aciub** |
| **Blockers** | None, or minimal user action needed |

No jargon walls; tables over long prose.

---

<h2 id="qimpl-chain" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">6. Execution chain (classic — chain 1)</h2>

When **`qimpl`** is active, resolve delegated rules to these **exact paths**:

| Step | Keyword | Rule file |
|------|---------|-----------|
| Plan | **`onlyref`** | `.cursor/rules/onlyref-refactor-plan-author-only.mdc` |
| Implement loop | **`aciub`** | `.cursor/rules/aciub-allow-continue-iterations-until-blocked.mdc` |
| Impl spine | **`implref`** / **`resumimpl`** | `.cursor/rules/implref-resumimpl-refactor-plan-followthrough.mdc` |

**TDD chain 2:** user must invoke **`qimpltdd`** instead — see `.cursor/rules/tdd/qimpltdd-quick-implement-refactor-plan.mdc`.

---

<h2 id="qimpl-stop" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">7. Stop conditions</h2>

Pause and engage the user only when:

- **Step 1** true ambiguity needs answers (multiple-choice sent).
- **aciub** / **implref** true blocker (build/tests unfixable, missing secrets, explicit scope cut, session cut per **implref** §3.1e).
- All plan scope **and** sidetracks are **`[X]`** — then step 4 and stop.

Resume: **`qimpl <same-plan-path>`** or **`aciub`** / **`resumimpl`** on the plan — classic chain only.

---

<h2 id="qimpl-self" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">8. Self-check (agent)</h2>

- [ ] User invoked **`qimpl`** (not **`qimpltdd`**).
- [ ] Step 1: MC questions **or** “No blocking ambiguities” + proceeded.
- [ ] Step 2: **onlyref** plan(s) with phased tests, DRY, and the **implref** comments-and-docs gate (executed in step 3, not only written into the plan).
- [ ] Step 3: **aciub** ran all phases without handoff spam.
- [ ] Step 4: layman closing table delivered.
